# pf anchor: reach deck-remote on ONE origin whether or not Tailscale is up.
#
# deck-remote terminates TLS itself on 127.0.0.1:8443 (a *.ts.net cert), which
# keeps it an unprivileged user agent. These rules redirect :443 to it so the
# phone always uses https://<host>.ts.net with NO port — the service worker and
# the Web Push subscription are bound to that exact origin, so a port change
# would mean a fresh PWA install and a fresh subscription.
#
# The source tables ARE the access control: a client outside them does not match
# the rdr, so it reaches :443 where nothing listens and the connection is
# refused. The bearer token remains the second gate.
#
# NOTE: pf rdr does not apply to traffic the host originates to itself, so
# curling https://<host>.ts.net/healthz FROM this Mac will not hit :8443 —
# test with `curl -k https://127.0.0.1:8443/healthz` locally and from the phone
# for the real path.

table <deckremote_ok> const { 100.64.0.0/10, 192.168.50.0/24 }
table <deckremote_ok6> const { fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 }

rdr pass on ! lo0 inet  proto tcp from <deckremote_ok>  to any port 443 -> 127.0.0.1 port 8443
rdr pass on ! lo0 inet6 proto tcp from <deckremote_ok6> to any port 443 -> ::1       port 8443
